        &nbsp;<blockquote>
          <p align="center"><font face="Tahoma" size="2">
          <img border="0" src="Logo.jpg"><br>
&nbsp;</font></p>
          <p align="left"><b><font face="Tahoma" size="2">
          <img border="0" src="Syyd.jpg" align="right">MEMBER POLICIES</font></b></p>
          <p align="left"><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><b>GUILD LEADER<br>
          </b>Our Guild Leader is Syyd (see picture at right), a retired Wizard.&nbsp; 
          Although he holds the title, the CoU is run by cooperation, and Syyd 
          will only be awakened to settle disputes<b> </b>which go unresolved or 
          for&nbsp; communications with other guilds.&nbsp; His role as guild 
          leader may come as a surprise to many, who previously believed Syyd to 
          be a taxi-cab or Nexus Scion.&nbsp; He's a man in a dress, and he's 
          proud.<br>
          <b><br>
          OFFICERS<br>
          </b>We have many officers at present.&nbsp; The purpose of our 
          officers it to provide leadership and assistance to members and 
          non-members in need.&nbsp; We have done our best to make sure that 
          officers are spread out across levels and across time zones so that 
          each part of our guild is represented in the final decision making 
          process.&nbsp; Our officers are not gentlemen.&nbsp; Our gentlemen are 
          not officers.<b><br>
          <br>
          MEMBERS<br>
          </b>Our membership comprises many levels, though most of our players 
          are level 50+.&nbsp; Members are not required to attend any raid or 
          event.&nbsp; Our only requirement is that members treat others 
          respectfully and that they do their best to enjoy themselves.<b>&nbsp;
          </b>Members who create alternate characters (alts) are welcome to have 
          them join the guild at any time.<b>&nbsp; </b>Any member is free to 
          come and go as they please, but will be subject upon leaving to the 
          five raid rule and approval process.&nbsp; Additionally, if you are 
          good looking, tall, troll, or have extremely pleasant breath, you can 
          expect to be treated better by your peers.&nbsp; If you are short, 
          have foul breath, and a nasty rash, your name is Aquin, and you are 
          already beloved by all.<b><br>
          <br>
          RECRUITING POLICY<br>
          </b>Typically, CoU is an entirely open guild, welcoming all interested 
          members.&nbsp; However, in order to maintain guild chemistry, there 
          may periodically be a recruitment freeze for a set duration of time.&nbsp; 
          During this period, officers may only guildinvite ALTS and RL friends 
          of members.&nbsp; Other members may be admitted only through 
          extenuating circumstances.<b><br>
          <br>
          </b>Officers performing a guild invite should tell at least two other 
          officers about the new member, notify the guild in guildchat in case 
          of any objections, and make the new recruit do the hokey pokey prior 
          to invitation.&nbsp; Each new member should be referred to the web 
          site, and told about our &quot;five raid rule&quot; for loot to prevent 
          confusion.&nbsp; Describing the five raid rule backwards, or in pig 
          latin may also add to their confusion, but will provide your 
          guildmates with amusement, and is acceptable.&nbsp; </font></p>
          <p align="left"><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><b>REMOVING A MEMBER<br>
          </b>Gnomes, dwarves, and other stinkers may be removed without notice, 
          unceremoniously, at the whim of officers.&nbsp; If someone needs to be 
          removed for a serious reason, at least two other officers will be 
          appraised of the decision before action is taken.&nbsp; If a member 
          decides to quit before he can removed, they will be scolded in 
          guildchat (despite their inability to hear) and ultimately told &quot;You 
          can't quit... You're FIRED!&quot;</font></p>
          <p align="left"><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><b><br>
          <br>
          LOOT POLICIES</b></font></p>
          <p align="left"><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><b>In GROUPS: </b><br>
          - If the group is made up entirely of guild members, we use the NBG 
          (need before greed) system. That means whoever needs it most gets it.<br>
          - If the group is not all guild members, all party members roll for 
          the item, and are eligible for it. Highest roll wins.<br>
          <br>
          <b>On RAIDS:<br>
          </b>- Only guild members who have attended at least five raids and/or 
          non guild raid members that were asked to come OUT OF NECESSITY may 
          roll for items.<br>
          - If an item drops that many can use, or that isn't of much use at 
          all, the loot master will call out for all classes that can use it to 
          roll. Highest roll wins. If no one rolls, the item will be re-lottoed, 
          with people being allowed to roll for an ALT.<br>
          - In instances of extremely high level, epic, or rare loot, the raid 
          leader and loot leader may assign loot to a present guild member, or 
          to a non-present guild member under extreme circumstances.<br>
&nbsp;</font></p>
          <p align="left"><font face="Tahoma" size="2">Want to change a policy 
          or add a new one?&nbsp; Bring it up on the PRIVATE FORUM.</font></p>
          <p><font face="Tahoma" size="2"><br>
&nbsp;</font></p>
          </blockquote>
